= Computation — Simple =

'''Computation''' is what happens when a system follows rules to change information or state.

A calculator performs a computation when it adds two numbers. A computer performs computations when it runs a [[Program (computing)/Simple|program]], searches data, draws an image, or sends a message.

A [[Algorithm/Simple|algorithm]] is a method for doing something. A program is a way of expressing behavior for a computer. A computation is the actual process of carrying out computational steps.

Computer scientists also study computation without choosing a particular computer. They use abstract models to ask questions such as:

* Can this problem be solved by any algorithm?
* How much time or memory would a solution need?
* Do two different kinds of computer have the same basic computational power?

Not everything that can be simulated by a computer is automatically a computer itself. A computer can simulate a storm, for example, without proving that the storm literally performs the same computation.

